{
  "Title": "ELSA-2026-102195:  openssh security, bug fix, and enhancement update (MODERATE)",
  "Description": "[9.9p1-34.0.1]\n- Upstream references found with /usr/bin/ssh [Orabug: 37824421]\n\n[9.9p1-34]\n- CVE-2026-106552: Fix arbitrary file write via directory traversal\n  during sftp recursive copy\n  Resolves: RHEL-286919\n- CVE-2026-106585: Fix DoS via oversized decompressed packets\n  Resolves: RHEL-286854\n- CVE-2026-106583: Fix command injection via unvalidated command-line username\n  Resolves: RHEL-286957\n- CVE-2026-106582: Fix compression side-channel by disabling L77 dictionary coder\n  Resolves: RHEL-286833\n- CVE-2026-106553: Fix credentials persisting after GSSAPI authentication attempt failure\n  Resolves: RHEL-286877\n- Fix resource leaks in krb5 and GSSAPI authentication\n  Related: RHEL-286877\n- Fix and enable the PKCS#11 URI tests\n  Related: RHEL-288515\n- Restores functionality of IdentitiesOnly=yes with PKCS#11 URI in IdentityFile\n  Resolves: RHEL-288515\n- Fix temporary lockout when trying to copy public ssh-keys with ssh-copy-id\n  Resolves: RHEL-288521",
